# Line endings are a repo property, not a per-developer git config.
#
# Without this file the repo happens to store LF only because contributors
# have core.autocrlf set correctly on their own machines. Anyone cloning
# without it commits CRLF, which shows up as a whole-file diff on the next
# edit. Storing and checking out LF everywhere makes it deterministic and
# matches what prettier/eslint expect.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never run line-ending conversion or text diffs on these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.pdf binary
*.mp4 binary
*.webm binary

# SVG is text and worth diffing, but it is authored, not hand-edited prose.
*.svg text eol=lf
